@startuml sequence-ghidra-analysis
' Method as reported by Sean Donnellan. No source/artifacts leave the isolated analysis boundary.
title Ghidra-assisted protocol analysis - separated Copilot roles
skinparam backgroundColor #fff/aaf
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #fff/aaf
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #fff/aaf
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #fff/aaf
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Sean Donnellan" as Sean
box "Steam Deck - isolated Ghidra analysis boundary" #fff-orange
  participant "Analysis Copilot" as Analysis
  participant "Ghidra MCP" as MCP
  participant "Ghidra project" as Ghidra
  database "Vendor binary\nread-only local mount" as Binary
end box
participant "Protocol-only notes" as Notes
participant "Implementation Copilot\nseparate session" as Implementer
participant "Rust repository" as Repo
participant "Wainlux K6" as K6

Sean -> Analysis : Ask a narrow protocol question
Analysis -> MCP : Query binary behavior in Ghidra
MCP -> Ghidra : Analyze inside container
Ghidra -> Binary : Read local binary
Binary --> Ghidra : Analysis input
Ghidra --> MCP : Tool result stays in analysis session
MCP --> Analysis : Evidence for protocol behavior
Analysis -> Notes : Write packet/response description only
note over Analysis,Ghidra
  Vendor source and Ghidra artifacts are not emitted
  through CLI, web UI or into the workspace.
  No screenshots, source text or analysis artifacts
  are handed to the implementation role.
end note

Sean -> Implementer : Provide protocol notes, packet captures\nand hardware observations
Implementer -> Repo : Independently implement and test Rust behavior
Sean -> K6 : Trigger and verify supervised hardware tests
K6 --> Sean : Physical observation
Sean -> Repo : Approve project decisions and record results

note over Analysis,Implementer
  Separate roles: the analysis Copilot could inspect code
  only inside Ghidra; the implementation Copilot did not
  access Ghidra, the binary or source.
end note
footer (C)2026 Sean Donnellan
@enduml
